hello and welcome to the new world of  your source for everything anime and  manga and today we are back to review  arc iv  of this black clover business being the  eye of the midnight sun and i suppose it  really was something of a direct sequel  to the royal capital arc that expands on  our big group of bad dudes and  dudettes and in a way that was really  great but i have a lot more questions  than i had before the first of which is  will you subscribe to the new world  review and like this video in order to  let me know if you  want more black clover stuff i try not  to read the comments of these videos due  to fear of spoilers so that's how we  need to run this operation now getting  into it as for the premise of the ark  the clover kingdom is still reeling from  the recent assault on the capital  questions are being asked traitors are  being posited and amongst all of this  astor is taking some well-earned time  off which inevitably leads to some time  on because manga gonna manga as we delve  deeper into the midnight sun group than  i thought we would anytime soon and  probably my favorite thing about the ark  is just how  damn smoothly it flows its events feel  very natural and we take a bit more time  to let things unfold i mean for example  in the previous two arcs we were very  suddenly thrown into things you know  asked to get stumped with a mission then  bam we are straight into action whereas  with this one tabitha elected to do the  opposite and astor was told to do  nothing which was a nice touch to begin  leading with a comedic blind date sort  of scenario  which led into meeting all of the kids  as well as gauche which then leads into  action to save the kids which then leads  into utter magical madness it's very  simple but the events of this arc flow  very well into one another nothing is  jarring and it just keeps building and  building to the point where we have what  is turned out to be the most  intense blind state of all time and i  think what greatly helps with that is  that the main group of villains were  established in the previous arc so we  didn't have to go through the basic  introductory phase and i must say  i do like the midnight sun guys a lot  more than i did previously although  maybe it's just these more specific  members and i guess licks needs to be  brought up pretty damn immediately  because he is kind of  single-handedly responsible for my  renewed interest in the group at first  he gives me a super strong griffith from  berserk sort of vibe you know this all  ornately beautiful  existence with overwhelmingly dark  intentions like her perversion of  aesthetic that impression changed pretty  rapidly though when valtos got hurt and  licht made this absolutely terrifying  face that broke his delightful facade  but showing that he legitimately cares  for his fellow  and i don't really know what to call  them cultist his fellow cultists  question mark doesn't matter though  because the camaraderie is there which  seems to be a running theme with the  midnight sun even right at the beginning  of the arc the two captured members say  something along the lines of when all  others betrayed us the master did  not we could never repay that with  betrayal and licks later expands on this  by referring to his group as the targets  of jealousy fear discrimination  persecution and theft which i don't know  does that essentially just make them  another incarnation of the black bulls  except that the primary difference would  be that the bulls choose to defy  societal standards whilst working within  the system whilst the eye of the  midnight sun wants to destroy the system  and replace it with their own more  subjectively equal system i shall call  it  magical socialism at least that's the  vibe i got and i do think that licht is  quite a good figurehead of that  although when it comes to their  technical goal i'm still kind of less  than convinced because if i understand  correctly what they need is the magic  rocks to put into a bigger magic rock  which will then turn everyone into super  mages which is a bit meh because i feel  like it means we're going to spend a lot  of time focused on finding objects that  will all inevitably come together in  favor of the antagonist anyways i don't  know just just do it with that said it  really doesn't matter too much though  because to say i'm hugely invested in  the plot of black clover right now would  be  an outright lie it's all about the  characters for me and speaking of  this arc only reinforced my initial  impression of the army as by far the  greatest character in the series this  man  is everything he is a dark magic sword  wielding badass with a phenomenal aspect  of humor in fact his comedy is what  sells me on him the most like i remember  there was this particular moment where  he was teaching astro about key which is  well that's something else but when  astor used it for the first time yami  was just all like  you actually managed to do it creepy get  away from me  and i obviously can't do the line  justice but i think every second thing  yami said had me laughing in addition to  that he also has what i consider to be  the best drawn action scenes in the  series thus far i love that in many  panels tabita elects to hide a lot of  yami's face  sometimes showing just a single eye it  takes away a lot of his humanity and  really makes him seem like a monster in  the dark and what's even cooler is that  xiaomi is directly equated to the power  of the wizard gang  not only by valtos but also licht who  states that the army was the second  person with the power to defeat him  which i find strange given that the end  of the arc introduces us to three other  characters whom licked claims are far  superior to him in combat but  it doesn't matter what matters is yami a  very obvious and appropriate name for a  dark magic user of course but yami also  introduces us to a very important  i think new concept being key which i am  led to believe is a completely separate  system to mana and in fact i think this  was even hinted at during the last arc  in retrospect yuna was almost certainly  using ki when all of his senses were  taken away by the  the witch woman right in terms of what  key actually is though well the one  piece fan within me just wants to call  it observation hockey it's the same sort  of effect only asta learnt at roughly  600 chapters before luffy did and  honestly i'm not quite sure how to feel  about it i do like it but i also feel  like we haven't quite gotten the hang of  basic magic use yet so introducing a new  system on top of that is  well it's very fast moving but as for  magic it continues to be expanded upon  and this arc highlights the importance  of matchups i quite like the idea that  certain types of magic are hard counted  by others in this kind of scissors paper  rock style system which is what we call  it in australia we don't do this rock  paper scissors nonsense and it was  really cool to see army's dark magic  interact with licks light magic and  oh god act like just means light in  german doesn't it i can't  believe it took me until right now this  moment mid-recording to notice that hm  so basically in this arc we had two  people fighting whose names were  literally light  and dark fantastic but it was nice to  see a sort of tired match up light and  dark countering each other in equal  measure coming equipped with their  inherent and polar opposite advantages  and disadvantages  magic is also getting a bit weird though  because there was a part of this arc  where the idea of transferring magical  power was very  very casually introduced and apparently  absolutely everyone can do it including  young children  which i don't know surely from here on  out the answer to every non-aster  related problem becomes if you're  injured then immediately follow your  magic into the nearest mage and turn  them into a supermage which  i guess is a good segue into gauche our  arc specific black bull focus  member guy who is the exact opposite of  the more carefree nature we've seen  expressed in the other members thus far  which is good that's very good actually  it's always nice to see a different  exploration although the sister complex  is pretty  heavy for me then again i don't have  siblings so i don't quite get that bond  but it does tend to border on the  the creepier side for me though however  i do find it quite interesting that the  other key player in this story threat is  a nun or sister  if you will so this man is just  surrounded by that sister complex at  every turn and just very briefly god  that nun was incredible as soon as i saw  those scars i knew she was serious  business and there was a great fun  generational aspect to her as well  having been fuego leon's teacher and all  but  back to gauche though his story was  quite satisfying mostly because his  change of heart came directly from his  sister like the last thing i wanted was  another situation where astor said a  sentence which instantly changed a core  personal flaw like what appeared to  happen with luck so it was great to see  that gauche's personal growth came from  the one person in the world that he  would  actually listen to and what's even  better is that after that we saw a great  example of a magic knight  leveling up in real time because a new  spell appeared in gosha's grimoire after  he had the realization of working with  others that sort of stuff is really  satisfying to me  and astor had a moment like that as well  actually there was this part where he  quoted fuego leon by stating that a  magic knight should always keep a cool  head and even though that didn't lead to  like a new spell  or anything it shows me that astor has  grown and that he is now much more  prepared to handle the world than he was  during the last arc so good  on him however when it comes to astor  there is something that i  quite profoundly hate which is his  ever-growing harem it's getting a bit  ridiculous now when it was noel a mimosa  well that was one thing but we now have  two other  females head over heels in love laster  being rebecca and marie the latter of  which  is very young and i'd even throw sally  in as well as someone who's certainly  obsessed with asda albeit on a very  different level and it just kind of  sucks it's by far the worst part of the  series and i feel like it's only going  to get worse  i mean when we have stuff like noel  dressing up as a maid just to spy on  astor's alleged and non-existent love  life that's very much where i check out  of the story for a while with astor  though something i do very much like  about him is how easy it is to have him  involved in conflicts that he really  should not be a part of but he has this  perfect excuse with anti-magic because  that's such a rare utility that can be  used to great effect whereas i feel like  in many other series it can be quite a  struggle to bring the protagonist into  battles like this because they really  have no business being there oh and we  also found  out asta's official rank which as of  right now is junior magic knight  third class although i maintain he's  much closer to an intermediate rank  about where leopold is but we cannot  conflate power with bureaucracy these  ranks are obviously more achievement  based than they are power based over  there it is good to have some sort of  solid footing for him though because now  it's only like what 17 or 18 more levels  to go until we reach the status of  wizard king oh and something i haven't  spoken about yet licht seems to be quite  intimately familiar with asta's grimoire  and his abilities his swords even have  names actually the demon slayer and the  demon dweller  sounds quite cool really although in the  end it turns out that they once belonged  to the ever mysterious  master because while licht is the leader  there exists an even greater master who  is maybe the actual leader i don't know  fun i'm looking forward to exploring  that a bit more maybe and as for going  into things a bit more these midnight  sun reinforcement  trio guys are quite fascinating aren't  they especially the one  named farna which just happens to be the  exact same name of mars childhood friend  and so there's absolutely no way that  they aren't the same person right i  would flip  every table within a 100 meter radius if  tarbata just used the exact same name  twice and  pretty much the exact same design for no  good reason and fauna would fit in quite  rightly with this group's theme  assumedly having been cast aside and  devalued by her own kingdom the evil  diamond kingdom damn diamonds so that  sounds like more good stock for some fun  personal conflict in the future with mr  diamond himself  but more importantly she has an adorable  salamander another spirit of the four  great attributes quite a terrifying  little pet really the other guy of  interest is mr copy magic which  i honestly don't remember if his name  was stated if it was sorry i just don't  remember  vana and the other guy's names were but  i like his design quite a bit though  it's sleek unique but tarbata has made  him well like  not overly pretty if that makes sense  which is unique because tarbeta does  have a habit of creating these very  pretty characters but mr copy man here  has this almost  underwhelmingly plain face which oddly  enough does make him stand apart in this  series of very well sculpted specimens  and at the end of the arc he is at the  center of all of the intrigue where it  is shockingly revealed  that he was one of the people present in  the captain's meeting as for which one  he was well  tabitha kind of breaks the fourth wall  there and even has the character  straight  so which one was me and at this stage  honestly i don't know the obvious guess  is the golden dawn leader because i  don't understand how  anybody anywhere at any time can trust  that face but at the same time  is that too obvious this guy is so damn  suspicious that he's making me second  guess  my own suspicion at the same time though  i really don't know who else it would be  maybe  one of the miscellaneous captains that  we really haven't gotten to know yet but  would that be underwhelming i don't know  though i've still got my eye on you  william  van gentz if that is indeed your real  name and if it is that's also highly  suspicious because vangen  sounds like vengeance and basically  every midnight suncultist in the series  seems to be driven by  vengeance but all in all another solid  arc for black clover this is usually the  point where i would have dropped a  series if i was feeling less than great  and whilst it does have a few flaws this  series continues to hold my interest  though with very strong characters and i  look forward to seeing where we end up  next but that pretty much does it for  this blind review of the eye of the  midnight sun arc and what do you guys  think please do leave your thoughts in  the comments below or even join my  discord server and if you are keen for  some more black clover content then  please to go and check out some of my  other videos or even subscribe to the  channel for very maybe black clover  goodness delivered straight into your  youtube feed but for now this has been  the new world review  and i'll see you next time

